  "identifier": "azt1d",
  "name": "AZT1D",
  "alternateName": [
    "AZT1D: A Real-World Dataset for Type 1 Diabetes"
  ],
  "description": "Real-world longitudinal dataset for type 1 diabetes management research from Mayo Clinic Arizona and Arizona State University. Contains 6–8 weeks of automated insulin delivery (AID) system data per participant across 25 individuals (13F/12M, age 27–80, mean 59), collected December 2023–April 2024. Modalities: continuous glucose monitoring (CGM), insulin pump records with granular bolus detail (total dose, bolus type, correction-specific amounts), carbohydrate intake, and device mode (regular, sleep, exercise). The granular bolus breakdown is the primary differentiator from other public T1D datasets such as OhioT1DM. Designed to support glucose prediction models, digital twin development, and personalised AID algorithm research. CC BY 4.0, v1 May 2025. Presented at IEEE-EMBS BSN 2025; arXiv 2506.14789.",
